# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SAFETY NET — this git repo's root is the HOME directory (/Users/robbiebutt).
# That is not intended; a relocation is planned. Until then, this file shields
# every untracked file in your home folder (.ssh, .aws, .config, .claude.json,
# shell history, Dropbox, etc.) from ever being staged by an accidental
# `git add -A` / `git add .` and pushed to GitHub.
#
# How it works: ignore EVERYTHING, then re-allow only the .gitignore itself.
# Files already committed stay tracked and continue to stage when modified —
# .gitignore does not un-track anything. To add a genuinely NEW file to this
# repo, use `git add -f <path>` deliberately.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/*
!/.gitignore
.gstack/
